@Harpush 

> I don't think this is correct. Returning a boolean just goes around the problem of not having types. I believe something like [#51878 (comment)](https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/51878#issuecomment-1973757043) should be the solution.

This is not supposed to replace any solution described in #51878. That issue describes a compile-time check, this issue describes a runtime check. Ideally we'd have both, but the compile-time check is non-trivial for reasons described there and does not seem likely to be implemented soon (hope I'm wrong), whereas this runtime check is trivial as you can see from my PR.
